    {
      "type": "entry",
      "wm-id": 2035,
      "wm-property": "in-reply-to",
      "wm-target": "http://localhost:8080/notes/fixture-note/",
      "url": "https://aaronparecki.com/notes-fixture-note-in-reply-to-2035",
      "published": "2026-08-30T16:25:00Z",
      "author": {
        "name": "Aaron Parecki",
        "url": "https://aaronparecki.com/",
        "photo": ""
      },
      "content": {
        "text": "The spec really is that small. One endpoint, one POST. The hard part is moderation, not delivery."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "entry",
      "wm-id": 2036,
      "wm-property": "in-reply-to",
      "wm-target": "http://localhost:8080/notes/fixture-note/",
      "url": "https://jacky.wtf/notes-fixture-note-in-reply-to-2036",
      "published": "2026-08-30T17:32:00Z",
      "author": {
        "name": "Jacky Alcine",
        "url": "https://jacky.wtf/",
        "photo": ""
      },
      "content": {
        "text": "Agreed \u2014 and the fact you can implement the receiving half in an afternoon is why it spread."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "entry",
